/*! @brief The XmlCDATASection object represents a CDATA section in a document

The XmlCDATASection interface is a subinterface of the XmlText interface and defines no properties or methods of its own. The text content of a CDATA Section can be accessed through the nodeValue property inherited from the XmlNode interface or the data property inherited from the XmlCharacterData interface.

Although an XmlCDATASection node can usually be treated as an XmlText node, note that the normalize method of XmlNode does not merge adjacent CDATA parts.

Use the createXmlCDATASection method of XmlDocument to create an XmlCDATASection.

A CDATA section contains text that is not parsed by the parser. Tags inside a CDATA section are not treated as markup, and entities are not expanded. Its main purpose is to include material such as XML fragments without escaping all delimiters.

The only delimiter recognized in a CDATA section is "]]>", which marks the end of the CDATA section. CDATA sections cannot be nested.
*/
interface XmlCDATASection : XmlText
{
};
